  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 861bc016933547642bf2de40bc14f38c, type: 3}
  m_Name: LiahEncounter
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Game.RunEncounters.EventEncounterData
  eventName: liah
  title: A Hut in the Jesterwoods
  fullText: Smoke rises from a hut at the forest's edge, within sound of the sea.
    An old woman sits mending nets with hands that shake. She doesn't look at your
    faces. She looks at the sword at Ayteel's hip, and her hands go still. "Steeldawn,"
    she says. "I haven't seen that light in sixty years."
  classIntroLines:
  - characterClass: 1
    text: The sword feels warm against Ayteel's side, as if it knows the voice.
  - characterClass: 3
    text: Faelin glances at Ayteel. Ayteel hasn't moved.
  - characterClass: 2
    text: 'Werlem feels her Grace before he understands it: old and patched, a soul
      mended once by a hand far stronger than hers.'
  options:
  - label: Tell her whose sword it is.
    classLabels:
    - characterClass: 1
      text: Tell her who you are.
    onlyForClass: 0
    hint: She already knows. She wants to hear it said.
    outcome: 0
    result:
      actions: []
      resultText: 
      classResultLines: []
      nextStepId: name
    check:
      source: 0
      stat: 8
      difficulty: 1
      introLine: 
    success:
      actions: []
      resultText: 
      classResultLines: []
      nextStepId: 
    failure:
      actions: []
      resultText: 
      classResultLines: []
      nextStepId: 
  - label: Buy smoked fish and move on.
    classLabels: []
    onlyForClass: 0
    hint: She sells what the sea gives. Pilgrims have to eat.
    outcome: 0
    result:
      actions:
      - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 458ddd8bb3e546fcb8516f212b723f15, type: 2}
      - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 1aee1acc903f4dbc94772f1e0bb7f4cf, type: 2}
      resultText: 'She sells you smoked fish for {chronos} Golden Chronos and watches
        you go. You eat well for the first time in days: +{health} health. Behind
        you, very quietly, she says a name.'
      classResultLines: []
      nextStepId: 
    check:
      source: 0
      stat: 8
      difficulty: 1
      introLine: 
    success:
      actions: []
      resultText: 
      classResultLines: []
      nextStepId: 
    failure:
      actions: []
      resultText: 
      classResultLines: []
      nextStepId: 
  - label: Ask about the Devourers.
    classLabels: []
    onlyForClass: 0
    hint: 'She speaks of them the way survivors do: low, as if they might hear.'
    outcome: 1
    result:
      actions: []
      resultText: 
      classResultLines: []
      nextStepId: 
    check:
      source: 0
      stat: 5
      difficulty: 1
      introLine: 
    success:
      actions:
      - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 68348fb29d2f456b93eb417b6ac8f3be, type: 2}
      resultText: '''They hunt by the soul''s light,'' she says, and teaches you
        the old way of hiding your Grace, the way children did in the Dark Age. You
        learn quickly. +{grace} Grace.'
      classResultLines: []
      nextStepId: 
    failure:
      actions:
      - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 41709384b00e4450a34be0af6f8ed3a9, type: 2}
      - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 68348fb29d2f456b93eb417b6ac8f3be, type: 2}
      resultText: 'She makes you practice hiding your Grace until your head pounds
        ({health} health). It''s worth it: +{grace} Grace.'
      classResultLines: []
      nextStepId: 
  steps:
  - id: name
    prompt: '''Alamoh,'' she whispers. ''Then you''ve come for the truth, or to spit
      on it like the rest.'''
    options:
    - label: '"The truth."'
      classLabels: []
      onlyForClass: 0
      hint: Sixty years she's waited for someone to ask.
      outcome: 0
      result:
        actions:
        - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 458ddd8bb3e546fcb8516f212b723f15, type: 2}
        - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 236eaa937233493d864037fee676f9fa, type: 2}
        resultText: '''I am Liah. His sister. When I was nine a Devourer ate my soul,
          and for six years I was nothing. A doll they fed and washed. Then my brother
          came home with a broken Seal in his hands and gave me back.'' Her voice
          hardens. ''They call it a sin. I call it my life.'' Before you go, you
          fill her pantry ({chronos} Golden Chronos). +{grace} Grace.'
        classResultLines:
        - characterClass: 1
          text: '''He broke it for you,'' Ayteel says. Liah looks at her a long time.
            ''Not only for me, child.'''
        - characterClass: 3
          text: Liah sees the Vidal crest on Faelin's quiver. 'The Grand Crusader
            told them the truth. Good. Gabien would have hated a lie told for him.'
        - characterClass: 2
          text: '''Kyro cried at the altar,'' she tells Werlem. ''He was the only
            one who didn''t pray. He was counting.'''
        nextStepId: 
      check:
        source: 0
        stat: 8
        difficulty: 1
        introLine: 
      success:
        actions: []
        resultText: 
        classResultLines: []
        nextStepId: 
      failure:
        actions: []
        resultText: 
        classResultLines: []
        nextStepId: 
    - label: '"To clear his name."'
      classLabels: []
      onlyForClass: 0
      hint: Names matter a great deal to the living.
      outcome: 0
      result:
        actions:
        - {fileID: 11400000, guid: a50302b2b9aa1ac49816da88e5bf2e2f, type: 2}
        - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 458ddd8bb3e546fcb8516f212b723f15, type: 2}
        resultText: '''Names.'' She laughs, and it turns into a cough. ''He never
          cared about his.'' [She presses something into your hand: {item}. ''He
          left this with me. He''d want it walking again.''] You leave her what you
          can spare for the winter: {chronos} Golden Chronos.'
        classResultLines: []
        nextStepId: 
      check:
        source: 0
        stat: 8
        difficulty: 1
        introLine: 
      success:
        actions: []
        resultText: 
        classResultLines: []
        nextStepId: 
      failure:
        actions: []
        resultText: 
        classResultLines: []
        nextStepId: 
  oncePerPilgrimage: 1
